sub completion | generate shell completion script
sub acp | start ACP (Agent Client Protocol) server
sub mcp | manage MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers
sub attach | attach to a running opencode server
sub run | run opencode with a message
sub debug | debugging and troubleshooting tools
sub providers alias=auth | manage AI providers and credentials [aliases: auth]
sub agent | manage agents
sub upgrade | upgrade opencode to the latest or a specific version
sub uninstall | uninstall opencode and remove all related files
sub serve | starts a headless opencode server
sub web | start opencode server and open web interface
sub models | list all available models
sub stats | show token usage and cost statistics
sub export | export session data as JSON
sub import | import session data from JSON file or URL
sub github | manage GitHub agent
sub pr | fetch and checkout a GitHub PR branch, then run opencode
sub session | manage sessions
sub plugin alias=plug | install plugin and update config [aliases: plug]
sub db | database tools
flag -h --help | show help [boolean]
flag -v --version | show version number [boolean]
flag --print-logs | print logs to stderr [boolean]
flag --log-level arg=values:DEBUG,INFO,WARN,ERROR | log level [string] [choices: "DEBUG", "INFO", "WARN", "ERROR
flag --pure | run without external plugins [boolean]
flag --port arg=none | port to listen on [number] [default: 0]
flag --hostname arg=none | hostname to listen on [string] [default: "127.0.0.1"]
flag --mdns | enable mDNS service discovery (defaults hostname to 0.0.0.0)
flag --mdns-domain arg=none | custom domain name for mDNS service (default: opencode.local
flag --cors arg=none | additional domains to allow for CORS [array] [default: []]
flag -m --model arg=none | model to use in the format of provider/model [string]
flag -c --continue | continue the last session [boolean]
flag -s --session arg=none | session id to continue [string]
flag --fork | fork the session when continuing (use with --continue or --s
flag --prompt arg=none | prompt to use [string]
flag --agent arg=none | agent to use [string]
flag --auto | auto-approve permissions that are not explicitly denied (dan
flag --mini | start the minimal interactive interface [boolean] [default:
flag --no-replay | disable mini session history replay on resume and after resi
flag --replay-limit arg=none | cap visible mini replay to the newest N messages [number]
